  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "Tables print 0x/1x/3x/4x reference numbers starting at 0001; subtract 1 for the wire address in each table."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": "1.38 and later",
 "source": {
  "title": "CONDUCTOR W1, CONDUCTOR W3 Technical Manual",
  "doc_number": "cond_w1w3-sw138-m (SW version 1.38)",
  "revision_date": "2015-06-15",
  "url": "https://www.swegon.com/siteassets/_products-documents-archive/waterborne-climate-systems/control-equipment/_en/cond_w1w3-sw138-m.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 65-70 (Modbus register W3)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Addresses are printed in Modicon form (0x coils, 1x discrete inputs, 3x input registers, 4x holding registers); wire address = number - 1 within each table.",
  "Sensor temperatures and battery voltage carry an explicit 1:10 scaling. Room temperature (3x0060), changeover temperature (3x0061) and the room-unit setpoint/flow readings (3x0031/3x0032) give a unit but no scaling, so they are left out.",
  "Left out: every temperature setpoint and temperature band in the holding table (frost guard 4x0023, TC1/TH1 normal and TC2/TH2 economy 4x0024-4x0027, night cool 4x0028, room-unit min/max 4x0029-4x0030, boost hysteresis 4x0033-4x0034, manual temperature 4x0063). The table gives °C or nothing and no scaling for them, while the input temperatures are marked 1:10, so the raw format is not settled.",
  "Also left out: PID Water Out and PID ChangeOver Out (3x0049/3x0050), whose -100 to 100 % range needs a signed format the manual never states.",
  "Also left out: the 16-register component name (ASCII byte order not given), application ID, serial number, software version and boot-year registers (no format given), and every Not used row.",
  "BMS port settings are menu parameters P_101 (address 1-247), P_102 (baud 9.6/19.2/38.4 k), P_103 (parity odd/even/none) and P_104 (stop bits).",
  "The manual prints 4x0046 and 4x0047 both as \"Stand-by flow EA\"; both are kept with the printed name.",
  "Input registers 3x0064-3x0066 are printed twice on the last page with identical content.",
  "The last W3 input-register page (3x0057-3x0066) is headed 'applies to software before 1.38' while every other W3 page says 'after 1.38'; the packed status copies 3x0063-3x0066 are kept because they match the W1 table."
 ],
